# Sample metadata: one row per pair of FASTQ files. Blank lines and # lines are ignored.
# The manual explains every column: https://ozankiratli.github.io/PoolSeqFlow/
#
# COLUMN KINDS, told apart by the prefix:
#   SampleID   required, unique. Must match the sample name readPattern takes from your FASTQ
#              names: with '*_R{1,2}.fq.gz', Sample1T1Rep1_R1.fq.gz gives Sample1T1Rep1.
#   RG_*       a read group tag: RG_Sample, RG_Library, RG_Platform, RG_PlatformUnit,
#              RG_Description, RG_Center, RG_Date, RG_FlowOrder. Closed list.
#   param_*    overrides a parameters.config setting for these rows: param_poolSize,
#              param_capMaxDepth, param_adapter1, param_adapter2. Closed list.
#   exp_*      what the experiment SET: exp_population, exp_time. Open list.
#   pt_*       a phenotype MEASURED on the pool: pt_resistance. Open list.
#   cov_*      a covariate measured alongside: cov_temperature. Open list.
#   anything   your own. Recorded, never interpreted.
#
# THE TWO THAT CHANGE A RESULT:
#   RG_Sample       the pool a row belongs to, and one column in the VCF. Rows sharing one are
#                   MERGED, reads pooled and depths added. Blank or absent: the row is its own
#                   pool. Step 0 prints the pooling before any compute is spent.
#   param_poolSize  individuals in the pool; sets its detection limit. Rows of one pool must
#                   give the SAME value. Absent: every pool uses the global poolSize.
#
# A value containing a comma must be quoted: "Pop1, coastal".
#
# The table below is an example: eight pairs, four pools, each sequenced twice. Replace it.
SampleID,RG_Sample,RG_Library,RG_Platform,RG_PlatformUnit,param_poolSize,exp_population,exp_time,pt_resistance,cov_temperature,sequencing_run
